{"name":"build-locale-pages.md","path":"jsdocs/shared/scripts/build/build-locale-pages.md","format":"markdown","html":"<article class=\"docs-md\"><h1 id=\"sharedscriptsbuildbuild-locale-pagesmjs\"><code>shared/scripts/build/build-locale-pages.mjs</code></h1>\n<p>Emits per-locale, per-route static index.html files into</p>\n<table><thead><tr><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody>\n<tr><td><strong>Source</strong></td><td><code>src/shared/scripts/build/build-locale-pages.mjs</code></td></tr>\n<tr><td><strong>UX surface</strong></td><td>The repo verbs — build, verify, test, docs, i18n, media, setup, scaffold.</td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<h2 id=\"members\">Members</h2>\n<h3 id=\"cyrillic_slug\"><code>CYRILLIC_SLUG</code></h3>\n<p>Russian Cyrillic → Latin transliteration — Cyrillic media labels would\notherwise slugify to '' and lose their deep-link URL. MUST stay\nbyte-identical to CYRILLIC_SLUG in core/utils/string.ts.</p>\n<h3 id=\"slugify\"><code>slugify</code></h3>\n<p>Media-slug transform — MUST match generate-sitemap.js's slugify byte for\nbyte: emitted /portfolio/<slug>/<media> file names have to line up with\nthe URLs the sitemap already lists (diacritics fold to ASCII).</p>\n<h3 id=\"esc\"><code>esc</code></h3>\n<p>Escape a string for use inside an HTML attribute or text node.</p>\n<h3 id=\"enc\"><code>enc</code></h3>\n<p>Percent-encodes a URL for markup/JSON-LD emission — bucket keys can\ncarry literal spaces ('brazilian leather/…', '…PARIS FASHION-WEEK…') and\nnon-ASCII, which break srcset candidate parsing (whitespace-separated\ngrammar) and RFC-3986-strict contexts (JSON-LD, sitemap locs). Mirrors\ncore/utils/media.ts encodeMediaUrl — that module uses @core aliases so\nthis standalone Node path can't import it. decodeURI-first keeps it\nidempotent on already-encoded input (encodeURI escapes '%' itself).</p>\n<h3 id=\"dec\"><code>dec</code></h3>\n<p>Reverses enc() for manifest-key lookups — bucket keys are stored raw,\nso a '%XX'-encoded URL must decode before <code>manifest.has</code>. Malformed\nescapes (a '%' not followed by two hex digits) make decodeURI throw, so\nthose short-circuit to the raw form.</p>\n<h3 id=\"todescription\"><code>toDescription</code></h3>\n<p>Strips markup from a translated rich-text string and compacts it into a\nmeta-description-sized plain-text snippet (≤160 chars, cut at a word\nboundary).   entities decode to regular spaces so the tag can sit\nin a content attribute.</p>\n<h3 id=\"breadcrumbentity\"><code>breadcrumbEntity</code></h3>\n<p>Ordered crumbs → BreadcrumbList entity (positions are 1-based per spec).</p>\n<h3 id=\"videoentity\"><code>videoEntity</code></h3>\n<p>VideoObject for one media descriptor — mp4 contentUrl + poster thumb.</p>\n<h3 id=\"module-scope\">(module scope)</h3>\n<p>Recursively yields every sections node that carries a <code>src</code>.</p>\n<h3 id=\"writecompressed\"><code>writeCompressed</code></h3>\n<p>Brotil + gzip siblings next to each emitted index.html (Firebase serves them).</p>\n<h3 id=\"localize\"><code>localize</code></h3>\n<p>Rewrites the English shell into a localized document.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>@param</code> {string} html - post-loader dist/index.html source</li>\n<li><code>@param</code> {object} o</li>\n<li><code>@param</code> {string} o.bcpLang - BCP-47 tag for <html lang> + og:locale alt</li>\n<li><code>@param</code> {string} o.ogLocale - og:locale value (xx_YY)</li>\n<li><code>@param</code> {string} o.title - document + social title</li>\n<li><code>@param</code> {string} o.description - meta description text</li>\n<li><code>@param</code> {string} o.url - this page's absolute URL</li>\n<li><code>@param</code> {string} [o.canonicalUrl] - canonical/og:url override for alias pages</li>\n<li><code>@param</code> {Array&lt;{bcp:string,url:string}&gt;} o.alternates - hreflang rows</li>\n<li><code>@param</code> {string} [o.image] - route-specific share image (project cover /</li>\n<li><code>@param</code> {Array<object>} [o.entities] - extra JSON-LD entities appended to</li>\n<li><code>@param</code> {string} [o.content] - prerendered body markup injected into</li>\n</ul>\n<h3 id=\"starmediadims\"><code>starMediaDims</code></h3>\n<p>Star-field dossier image dims cache — image URL → <code> width=\"W\" height=\"H\"</code>\nattribute fragment, seeded by <code>prefetchStarMediaDims</code> (dossier JSONs store\nno intrinsic size, so each unique CDN image is probed once via a small\nrange request and shared across all 15 locales).</p>\n<h3 id=\"dims_probe_bytes\"><code>DIMS_PROBE_BYTES</code></h3>\n<p>Bytes fetched per image-dims probe — SOF/IHDR headers live in the head.</p>\n<h3 id=\"scanimagedims\"><code>scanImageDims</code></h3>\n<p>Scans an image header for intrinsic dims — PNG IHDR (8-byte signature)\nor JPEG SOFn marker walk (FFD8 + length-prefixed segments; SOF markers\nare C0–CF except DHT/DAC/RST: C4, C8, CC). Returns [w, h] or null.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>@param</code> {Buffer} buf - head bytes of the image</li>\n</ul>\n<h3 id=\"livetranslations\"><code>liveTranslations</code></h3>\n<p>Live <code>translations</code> node pulled from the RTDB by prefetchTranslations().\nWhen set, buildLocalePages emits current per-locale CMS text instead of\nthe committed database.json snapshot (which lags behind content edits —\nthe exact gap that made localized pages render English/fallback text).</p>\n<h3 id=\"module-scope\">(module scope)</h3>\n<p>Fetches the live <code>translations</code> node once per build so every prerendered\npage carries the per-locale text authors actually published. Offline or\nunreachable host → warn and keep the database.json snapshot as the source.</p>\n<h3 id=\"module-scope\">(module scope)</h3>\n<p>Probes every unique star-field dossier image once (64 KB range request\neach) so emitted <img> tags carry real width/height attrs — the\nlazy-media CLS budget flagged the bare imgs. Failures are silent:\na missing probe just emits the attr-less tag it always did.</p>\n<h3 id=\"buildlocalepages\"><code>buildLocalePages</code></h3>\n<p>Generates all localized pages under <code>distDir</code>. When <code>template</code> is omitted\nthe post-loader dist/index.html is read from disk; when provided (the\nbuild orchestrator's in-memory copy) the localized root document is\nreturned so the caller can run its own compress/SW-stamp pass.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>@param</code> {string} distDir - absolute dist path</li>\n<li><code>@param</code> {string} [template] - shell HTML; defaults to dist/index.html on disk</li>\n<li><code>@returns</code> {{html: string, written: number, locales: number}} localized root html + counts</li>\n</ul>\n<h3 id=\"t\"><code>t</code></h3>\n<p>Per-locale lookup with English fallback (mirrors runtime appText).</p>\n<h3 id=\"firstpara\"><code>firstPara</code></h3>\n<p>Recursively finds the first paragraph string inside a nested sections payload.</p>\n<h3 id=\"projectentities\"><code>projectEntities</code></h3>\n<p>Full rich-media graph for one project page — Article + media\nItemList (entries deep-link to the emitted /portfolio/<p>/<media>\nURLs; the SPA serves every labelled media slug) + one VideoObject\nper video. Mirrors runtime generateProjectSchema.</p>\n<h3 id=\"projectimageof\"><code>projectImageOf</code></h3>\n<p>Cover share-image for a project — uncompressed jpg or video poster.</p>\n<h3 id=\"homeentities\"><code>homeEntities</code></h3>\n<p>Carousel ItemList for locale home pages — portfolio tiles → covers.</p>\n<h3 id=\"richparagraphs\"><code>richParagraphs</code></h3>\n<p>Authored rich-text array → <p> markup (trusted CMS html).</p>\n<h3 id=\"leafparagraphs\"><code>leafParagraphs</code></h3>\n<p>Every authored leaf string under a CMS node → <p> markup (trusted CMS\nhtml). Experience pages carry their copy as UI labels rather than a\nsingle description field — walking the whole object guarantees none of\nthe authored text is left JavaScript-only. <code>skip</code> drops keys already\nrendered as headings.</p>\n<h3 id=\"contactblock\"><code>contactBlock</code></h3>\n<p>Contact block — channel links + legal links from components.contact.</p>\n<h3 id=\"mediafigure\"><code>mediaFigure</code></h3>\n<p>One media item as crawlable markup — the figure's <img> carries the\nbest-quality source itself (uncompressed pass preferred) so crawlers\nand no-JS viewers index the full-resolution asset, not the thumb;\nthe caption links to the same source as a first-class crawl target.\n<code>deepHref</code> wraps the media in the /portfolio/<p>/<media> deep link.</p>\n<h3 id=\"homecontent\"><code>homeContent</code></h3>\n<p>Home page content — about bio + mentions + portfolio mosaic + contact.</p>\n<h3 id=\"legalcontent\"><code>legalContent</code></h3>\n<p>Legal page content — title + every authored section.</p>\n<h3 id=\"projectcontent\"><code>projectContent</code></h3>\n<p>Project interna — title, hero cover, all section text + every figure.</p>\n<h3 id=\"mediacontent\"><code>mediaContent</code></h3>\n<p>Media-modal deep link — the single asset + its caption + project context.</p>\n<h3 id=\"experiencecontent\"><code>experienceContent</code></h3>\n<p>Experience page content — title + every authored label/copy leaf.</p>\n<h3 id=\"animationscontent\"><code>animationsContent</code></h3>\n<p>Animations-reference hub — title + intro + every animation record's\nalt/longdesc as a definition list. The static mirror of the runtime\n<view-animations> listing: crawlers, AI agents and reader mode read the\nsame components.animations records without running JavaScript.</p>\n<h3 id=\"readstarbody\"><code>readStarBody</code></h3>\n<p>Star-field body dossier JSON — locale file with English fallback.</p>\n<h3 id=\"starbodycontent\"><code>starBodyContent</code></h3>\n<p>Star-field body page — dossier text, facts table, credited media.</p>\n<h3 id=\"starindexcontent\"><code>starIndexContent</code></h3>\n<p>Star-field index — description + the full localized body catalog.</p>\n<h3 id=\"pagenamefromtitle\"><code>pageNameFromTitle</code></h3>\n<p>/** Strips the <code>Luis Krötz | </code> prefix / <code> | Luis Krötz</code> suffix for crumb names.</p>\n<h3 id=\"mediarowsof\"><code>mediaRowsOf</code></h3>\n<p>Labelled-media {slug,label,media} rows of a project — mirrors\ngenerate-sitemap's walk and the runtime modal: every labelled item with\na src is addressable through /portfolio/<slug>/<media>.</p>\n<h3 id=\"routesfor\"><code>routesFor</code></h3>\n<p>Route table: relative path → title, localized description,\ncanonical-equivalent alternates path, optional canonical override.\n<code>path</code> is the emitted file path relative to its base (en → dist/,\nothers → dist/langs/); en home yields '' — dist/index.html is\nalready written by the root pass.</p>\n<h3 id=\"syncfirebaserewrites\"><code>syncFirebaseRewrites</code></h3>\n<p>Regenerates the <code>hosting.rewrites</code> + <code>hosting.redirects</code> blocks in\nfirebase.json. Rewrites keep the public locale URLs (<code>/br</code>, <code>/br/sobre</code>,\n…) serving the pages emitted under <code>dist/langs/&lt;loc&gt;/…</code> — destinations\nare single files (no glob capture), so the table enumerates every route\nthe same way <code>routesFor</code> does. Redirects 301 every noncanonical alias the\nrouter accepts — legacy project slugs (PROJECT_ALIASES incl. media deep\nlinks), English-segment routes under a locale prefix, <code>/space-playground</code>\nand <code>/&lt;loc&gt;/docs</code> — onto their canonical paths so crawlers consolidate\nonto the sitemap surface instead of indexing alias URLs. Preserves every\nnon-rewrite/non-redirect hosting key and the meta/CMS/SPA-catch-all\nentries declared in <code>STATIC_REWRITES</code>/<code>SPA_REWRITES</code>.</p>\n<h3 id=\"meta_file_rewrites\"><code>META_FILE_REWRITES</code></h3>\n<p><code>, </code>/portfolio/${canonical}/:splat`)</p>\n<pre><code>for (const loc of VALID_LANGS) {\n  if (loc === 'en') continue\n\n  addRedirect(`/${loc}/portfolio/${alias}`, `/${loc}/portfolio/${canonical}`)\n  addRedirect(`/${loc}/portfolio/${alias}/**`, `/${loc}/portfolio/${canonical}/:splat`)\n}\n</code></pre>\n<p>}</p>\n<p>// English legacy legal segments → canonical English slugs.\naddRedirect('/privacy', <code>/${enSlugs.privacy}</code>)\naddRedirect('/terms', <code>/${enSlugs.terms}</code>)</p>\n<p>// <code>/space-playground</code> → the locale's earthPlayground slug (en included).\naddRedirect('/space-playground', <code>/${enSlugs.earthPlayground}</code>)</p>\n<p>for (const loc of VALID_LANGS) {\nif (loc === 'en') continue</p>\n<pre><code>const slugs = LANG_SLUGS[loc] || {}\n\n// English-segment + legacy legal aliases under the locale prefix.\nfor (const [aliases, key] of [\n  [['privacy', 'privacy-policy'], 'privacy'],\n  [['gdpr'], 'gdpr'],\n  [['terms', 'terms-of-use'], 'terms'],\n  [['license'], 'license'],\n  [['about'], 'about'],\n  [['contact'], 'contact'],\n]) {\n  for (const alias of aliases) {\n    addRedirect(`/${loc}/${alias}`, `/${loc}/${slugs[key] || enSlugs[key]}`)\n  }\n}\n\n// English-segment experience aliases → localized canonical slugs.\nfor (const alias of ['earth-playground', 'space-playground']) {\n  addRedirect(`/${loc}/${alias}`, `/${loc}/${slugs.earthPlayground || enSlugs.earthPlayground}`)\n}\n\nconst sfTarget = `/${loc}/${slugs.starField || enSlugs.starField}`\n\naddRedirect(`/${loc}/star-field-experiment`, sfTarget)\naddRedirect(`/${loc}/star-field-experiment/**`, `${sfTarget}/:splat`)\n\n// English-segment animations alias → localized canonical slug.\naddRedirect(\n  `/${loc}/${enSlugs.animations}`,\n  `/${loc}/${slugs.animations || enSlugs.animations}`\n)\n\n// Docs are English-only — a locale-prefixed docs URL canonicalizes to\n// the unprefixed route, so it redirects rather than rendering.\naddRedirect(`/${loc}/docs`, '/docs')\naddRedirect(`/${loc}/docs/**`, '/docs/:splat')\n</code></pre>\n<p>}</p>\n<p>cfg.hosting.redirects = redirects</p>\n<p>fs.writeFileSync(firebasePath, <code>${JSON.stringify(cfg, null, 2)}\\n</code>)\n}</p>\n<p>/** Rewrites that sit before the locale table — meta files moved into\npublic/meta/ keep their root URLs through these entries. Per-locale\nsitemap files and localized agent-readable files (robots/urllist/llms/\nai-catalog under /meta/<loc>/) keep their <code>/&lt;loc&gt;/&lt;file&gt;</code> URLs.</p>\n<h3 id=\"spa_rewrites\"><code>SPA_REWRITES</code></h3>\n<p>CMS + SPA catch-all — always last.</p>\n</article>","mtime":"2026-10-20T23:20:23.686Z"}